WEBVTT

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.960
Look, turn around now

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.300
but things like chances won't be there anymore.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.760
That's what some people will tell you,

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:41.020
but there are just times when you can't move at all.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.480
Yes, everything I say

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:54.950
is for your sake.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.450
Sorry, but

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.740
I won't consent easily

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:05.620
to things I don't accept.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:12.630
Even if I can get by that moment with a lie

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.720
I'll end up regretting it afterwards.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.510
Whether it's the past or the future

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.600
or, of course, the present,

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:25.020
I am the one that has to shoulder it.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:29.690
You'll understand the meaning to everything afterwards.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.310
So let's worry!

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:33.940
even if you don't understand them now,

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.610
whether it has to do with pain, fortune or secrets.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.990
So don't cry, let's hold each other as we go

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.500
forever-

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:52.250
because it's my life.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:50.960
last frame of Manabi Straight! logo

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:01.940
September 13th, 2035.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:09.080
The new Student Council office was complete.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.950
September 14th of the same year.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:18.330
The judgment day for the School Fair revival petition.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.540
The percentage of petition we got...

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.300
...was 76%.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:29.790
As the condition for holding
the Seioh School Fair of 70% was passed,

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:34.990
an urgent joint meeting between the two schools, Seioh High School and Aikoh High School,

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.770
was held, where officials met to discuss this matter.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.830
With the approval of a number of conditions,

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:48.220
the holding of the Seioh School Fair was accepted.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.000
September 18th of the same year.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.880
Under the supervision of Aikoh High School
Student Council President Kakuzawa Takako,

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:01.450
the Seioh School Fair operations headquarters was established.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:08.860
Keeping the catch phrase of "From friends to buddies" and the concept of students running their own booths,

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.910
we began to consider more specific plans.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.200
September 21st of the same year.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.840
We turned in the proposal plan
for the 82nd Seioh School Fair to school officials.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.390
With amendments added,

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:25.120
the proposal plan was accepted
September 22nd of the same year.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:30.420
The preparations for the Seioh School Fair began.

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:37.680
Although we encountered many troubles due to the relatively short amount of preparation time,

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:41.900
Exit

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:43.750
progress went smoothly thanks to the operations HQ's close interaction with all students.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.830
Additionally, although her participation was limited to after-school time,

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.570
without Student Council President Kakuzawa Takako's assistance,

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:53.450
we would not have achieved our plans,

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:55.540
and I make special note of it here.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:56.390
And finally...

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:01.480
...On October 19th, 2035.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.700
I'll be going home first.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.190
Thanks for your help!

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.150
Wow, it's pitch dark already.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:09.820
Shoot!

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.330
We... We made it...

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.680
At 8:06:40 P.M.,

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:32.300
Preparations for the 82nd Seioh School Fair were complete.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:44.690
Get home safely, okay?

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.180
Okay.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.580
Let's head home.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.070
This isn't a dream, right?

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.490
Yeah.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:03.840
This isn't a dream.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.070
It's happening tomorrow, right?

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.590
Yup, tomorrow.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.060
Hey.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.090
Can I say something weird?

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.570
I don't want to go home tonight!

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.100
Yeah!

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.980
Hey, Manabi-chan.

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:31.210
Hm?

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.560
I've always wanted to know.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.900
About?

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:40.980
I've been wondering how the world appears to you, Manabi-chan.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:47.870
In our boring everyday lives, you always find something exciting and wonderful.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:53.280
I'm sure your eyes see a much different world than mine do, right?

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.790
I've wondered what kind of world you see.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:58.730
But you...

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:04.720
But you, Manabi-chan,

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:09.190
I can see it now.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.700
I can see it, too.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:25.050
In a big, big universe,

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.600
on a tiny planet,

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:30.070
there was a high school called Seioh.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:33.250
And on the rooftop of that high school,

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:36.140
there was a very, very small Student Council office,

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:40.470
where five girls laughed,

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:41.590
got angry,

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:43.410
cried,

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.850
and spent their days.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:52.020
The Student Council office is gone now,

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:56.160
and the girls will eventually graduate from the school.

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:01.170
But...

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.140
I'll never forget.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:12.220
I'll never forget this night.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:22.820
I love all of you.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:44.800
Here we go!!!

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.280
Yeah!!

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:53.530
I'd like to see your entry tickets now.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.250
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:56.960
Thank you.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.540
Is that really okay?

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:22.960
Yes, okay, okay.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.720
Then, we'll go with that.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:27.650
Thank you ~desu!

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.500
Mic test, one more time.

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:32.680
Man, but...

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.830
HQ sure has nothing to do.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:41.790
That just means our executive staff is doing a fine job.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.380
I want to go check out the fair...

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:43.760
No.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.760
It's okay, right?

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.130
Take me around.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:48.770
It's oka-

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:53.770
Tenchu.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:53.770
Note: Tenchuu means "punishment from God"

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:57.150
Hello?

00:08:57.150 --> 00:09:00.450
It seems like some suspicious guests have sneaked in?

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.270
It must be this!

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.530
Hold them for a bit more.

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:09.070
Mu-chi will head over right away.

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:12.700
I'm really sorry, but please wait a bit longer.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:13.500
Huh?!

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.690
This ticket is authentic, yo!

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:16.960
Get outta ma' way!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.550
My...

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:23.590
Things getting heated already at the reception?

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.310
You gotta problem with that?!

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:27.800
Don't be talkin' to us like that!

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.890
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:31.690
O-owwww!!!

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:32.980
You girls okay?

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.100
Y... Yes.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:41.530
Could you tell me how to get
to the School Fair's executive HQ?

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:43.250
Ah, I do have a ticket.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.990
Don't be getting cocky-

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.570
Tenchu!!!

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.660
I do not know who you are, but thanks for helping us.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.220
Uehara Mutsuki-san.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.200
I could tell right away.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:10:01.600
She always said you were a very, very energetic cute girl with short hair.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.740
C-Cute, eh?

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.720
Don't be fooled.

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:14.180
This naughty brother is in a fiery love affair with an older lady without telling his family.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.980
Takefumi-kun!

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:18.470
Hello, Kyoko-san.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.120
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:23.000
I really had a hard time putting on my makeup.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.270
WHY YOU?!?!

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:25.830
Question.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:29.030
Did you come today as Aikoh's superintendent?

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:32.820
Or as Kiyokawa Kyoko?

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:36.650
Of course, as the older lady, Kiyokawa Kyoko.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:37.080
Go home.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:42.180
You have now been expelled from this fair by the special authority of the Student Council President!

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:44.110
Security! There's a bad guy here!

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.740
God, calm down.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.080
What you're saying doesn't make sense.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.420
Things sure look fun here.

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:52.860
Takako-san!

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:07.850
Please, have this.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.950
Please enjoy your time.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:17.380
The truth is you came as
Aikoh's superintendent, right?

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:20.430
You came to see their answer.

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:23.830
The answer Manabi and her friends came up with.

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:30.670
I may have looked too far ahead.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:34.050
In this age of declining births,

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:37.940
I wondered whether there was any meaning to a School Fair just about fun.

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:40.560
If we don't find something more meaningful,

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:43.000
then there would no longer be any point of going to school.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.400
That was what I thought.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:46.020
But...

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.850
There's something that needs to be said,

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.410
Something very important, most likely.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.380
But I can't say it well,

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:57.240
So I'm going to shout out this song!

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:08.140
We had fights,

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.500
We even had days we didn't talk to each other, right?

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.570
But, for always

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:14.980
Being my buddy until now, I wanna thank you!

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:19.680
There might be no meaning to sunsets, but

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:23.500
I'll never forget

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.260
The sunset...

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.810
That I saw with you.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.990
Promise me

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:38.340
That as time goes by, someday,

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.840
We might be under different skies,

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:44.140
But if we get lost,

00:12:44.140 --> 00:12:47.470
Call each other's name and

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:54.040
Let us meet again under these cherry blossoms.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:57.970
Thank you, Takako-san!!!

00:12:57.970 --> 00:13:02.860
I-I guess it was worth bringing food if it makes you that happy.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.990
What you say rubs me the wrong way.

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.300
Heck, we have complete opposite personalities to begin with.

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:07.190
I wanted to see the costume parade at noon...

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.430
But, for always

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:08.340
Control yourself, control yourself.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.840
Being an idiot until now, I wanna thank you!

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.690
Apple candy-

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:10.260
Control yourself, control yourself.

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:14.680
I never really believed in "eternity",

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:14.720
We worked so hard for this, yet we can't
be in it ourselves. That doesn't make sense!

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:18.370
But I will never, ever

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:18.450
That's the fate of Student Council officers, Manabi-san.

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:22.140
Forget about...

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:19.780
That's true.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:23.470
But are you satisfied with that, Kakuzawa-san?

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.670
Right...

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.640
My feelings right now.

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.880
The party will end,

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:33.230
And as time goes by, someday,

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:34.510
Taka-chan?

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:36.710
We might be under different skies.

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:36.590
It's okay, just try it.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:39.030
But if we're taking backward steps,

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:42.300
Call each other's name and

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:49.480
Let us meet again under these cherry blossoms.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:00.950
Can you hear it?

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.660
I can.

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:10.010
I didn't even understand the meaning of "friends".

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:05.360
Yeah.

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.100
Not bad.

00:14:07.100 --> 00:14:09.980
This works, too, I guess.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:10.920
Right?

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.510
A bad person like me,

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:14.030
Thank you.

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:17.940
Right now...

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:19.930
You taught me this, Manabi-san.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.980
I can say it...

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:22.620
To picture it.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.520
"Thanks my friend!"

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.700
Promise me

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:24.880
And to realize that picture.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:28.050
That as time goes by, someday,

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.290
Now, I understand it, too.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.580
We might be under different skies,

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.860
But if we get lost,

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:37.160
Call each other's name and

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:45.230
Let us meet again under these cherry blossoms.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.580
Lalalalalalalala~

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:53.750
Lalalalalalalalalalala la~

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.710
We will meet again

00:14:56.710 --> 00:15:02.540
In this promised place under these cherry blossoms.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:18.160
HQ stayed peaceful until the end.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.860
Is this really okay?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:29.040
For teachers to help a student-operated School Fair?

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.130
What's wrong with that?

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.360
It's almost the end anyway.

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:33.940
You're right.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:39.850
Hurry, hurry!

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:39.850
What? What?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.230
Ah, there she is.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.050
Over here, over here!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:49.310
So, everyone in the audience!
Thanks for your support today!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:51.880
We're down to our final song,

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:55.450
so could I say something first?

00:15:55.450 --> 00:16:00.510
Umm, we had the greatest of times thanks to you all!

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:01.990
Thank you!

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:06.330
But the person that we want to thank the most...

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.120
...is you, Amamiya Manami-san!

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.630
If it wasn't for you,

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:16.740
we wouldn't be able to
sing our songs to everyone today.

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.980
Come on, go, go!

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:37.300
Well then, let's have our Student Council President sing the last song to end our day!

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.120
EHHHHH?!

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:45.300
Just sing whatever you want to sing; we'll do the accompaniment.

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.500
B-But...

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:14.110
Live the present moment, the season of encounters.

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:28.140
The bright sunlight, the gathering of dreams.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:35.410
The miracle where people walk through the same youth.

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:46.040
Cherry-blossom colored futures fly into the sky.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:18:00.190
Ah, the cheerful sounds of Seioh!

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:14.780
Ah, let it resonate through Seioh's garden!

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:29.490
When we shine, we shine with our friends.

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:58.880
Live the present moment, inside this happiness.

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:04.400
The bright sunlight, the gathering of the wind.

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:08.180
The burning love passion with

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:16.840
The hope-colored girls fly into the sky.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:24.540
Ah, the days of love at Seioh!

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:31.170
Ah, grow up inside Seioh's garden!

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:39.170
When we shine, we shine with our friends.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:05.630
Ah, the green leaves we look up to are far away.

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:12.260
Ah, when we get a hold of them, for sure, for sure,

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:21.770
When we shine, we shine with our friends.

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:52.570
But...

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:59.770
Those girls put out their lives to realize this School Fair and never turned back.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:05.530
Unlike the money and responsibilities once they enter society,

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:09.830
I thought things like doing
the best they can, rebelling,

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:13.250
and having all this passion...
these are things only students can experience.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:14.470
Is that not right?

00:21:15.360 --> 00:21:24.440
Indeed, if you think about it, this year's
School Fair isn't much different from last year's.

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:28.940
But, I still think this year's School Fair is special.

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:34.690
For it was a School Fair the students won back...

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:37.420
The last School Fair of Seioh High School.

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:04.850
I love you all!

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:17.300
We're still at the very beginning of things.

00:22:19.190 --> 00:22:24.050
Even the thousand-mile road starts with a first step.

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:30.980
There's a first time for everyone,

00:22:31.190 --> 00:22:38.520
so take it on fearlessly - that's the best way to go

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:47.800
I'm glad I chose a path I love,

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:55.010
so thank you, God.

00:22:57.820 --> 00:23:03.310
I want to treasure my luck right now

00:23:03.530 --> 00:23:06.610
And stay happy on the way.

00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:10.450
Come on, let's ride on the momentum

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:13.240
Bang！Bang！Bang！

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:15.410
That's right, Lucky!

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:19.000
Now is the time, happy!

00:23:19.060 --> 00:23:22.130
Grab your chances

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:27.300
And live your lives to the fullest...
